export const RECEIPT_0_18_0_ISSUE_646 = "## Resolution\n\n## Resolution\n\nThe W1 inventory resolves the surface into three distinct contracts; it rejects the\nsingle vague idea that one close gate currently protects every Soma mutation.\n\n1. **Work-graph completion is gated only through `soma graph close`.** The CLI\n   derives the receipt and calls `graph.close`; `WorkGraph.close` re-reads the\n   node and runs `assertClosable` immediately before the GitHub receipt-comment\n   and state-close mutation. GitHub's native PR/issue auto-close is outside that\n   path. `soma graph audit` detects receipt-less closed nodes but deliberately\n   does not repair them. Therefore tracker state is not a W1 completion fact.\n\n2. **Admitted durable memory has governed write paths, not work-graph receipts.**\n   `write`, `verify`, `used`, and assistant-trust consolidation merges route\n   through mutation governance and `writeNotesAtomically`, which couples the\n   note mutation to an event append on ordinary failure. This is best-effort, not\n   crash-atomic: a hard kill can leave an orphaned file/event gap. Importers and\n   operational telemetry have separate confinement or append-only contracts and\n   must never be confused with proof that a work item completed.\n\n3. **The enforcement artifact is not yet independent or uniformly identified.**\n   The current Claude, Codex, and Grok hook shapes invoke a configured\n   `trustedSomaRepo`; on this machine the Claude policy guard points at the\n   editable Soma worktree even though `~/.claude/bin/soma` points to Arc's\n   installed tree. A transient source failure can therefore fail-close every\n   repair tool. Private roots are likewise resolved from a loader-safe central\n   table rather than being mechanically proven equal to all adapter install and\n   hook declarations.\n\n### W1 invariant\n\nA Soma consumer may treat a work item as **complete** only when its authoritative\nclose write was preceded in the same operation by `assertClosable` on a freshly\nread node and produced a durable receipt. It may treat an admitted durable-memory\nmutation as **committed** only when it passed the appropriate governance resolution\nand its event-coupled write completed; crash/orphan cases remain explicit audit\nexceptions, never silent success. Tracker closure, a raw file change, and a\npolicy/telemetry event alone are diagnostics, not completion evidence.\n\n### W1 contract requirements now exposed\n\n- Completion consumers and decision projections must require a receipt; receipt-less\n  tracker closes may be reported only as non-completion diagnostics.\n- The guard must execute a pinned, independently installed artifact and record its\n  identity/freshness with each protected decision; guard-load failure stays\n  fail-closed but recovery cannot depend on that same failed artifact.\n- One loader-safe adapter-owned private-root fact must be checked for equality across\n  install specs, projected hook config, and policy evaluation for every substrate.\n- W1's implementation boundary is the consuming write point: the graph close state\n  mutation, governed durable-note writes, and policy decisions that authorize their\n  protected paths. It is not a blanket rewrite of every operational event/importer.\n\n### Evidence consulted\n\n- Current HEAD: `src/work-graph.ts`, `src/cli/graph.ts`,\n  `src/work-graph-github.ts`, `src/memory-write.ts`,\n  `src/policy-audit.ts`, `src/projection-private-roots.ts`, and Claude/Codex/\n  Grok hook configs and entrypoints.\n- Existing issue evidence: #596, #600, #601 (including its correction), #616, and\n  #640. Historical claims about one universal installed runtime were not accepted\n  where current configuration contradicted them.\n\n## Close receipt\n\n- **checkpoint:** `cp-evolution-w1-inventory`\n- **gist:** Completion requires a receipt at the close write; durable-memory commits require governance plus an event; tracker state and raw changes are diagnostics, while guard artifacts and private roots still need binding.\n- **closed by:** jcfischer\n- **closed with:** soma 0.18.0 @ fe6be2a (dev tree)\n- **at:** 2026-08-24T12:39:50.580Z\n- **attestation:** `unverified`\n\n### Evidence\n\n\n### Attestation facts\n\n```json\n{\n  \"backendCapability\": \"verifiable\",\n  \"confinement\": {\n    \"checked\": true,\n    \"reachableIdentities\": [\n      \"jcfischer\",\n      \"keychain:gh:github.com\"\n    ],\n    \"at\": \"2026-08-24T12:39:49.984Z\",\n    \"probes\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"gh auth status (token env stripped)\",\n        \"observed\": \"exit 0; identities: jcfischer\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"gh auth token (token env stripped)\",\n        \"observed\": \"printed a credential\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"security find-generic-password -s gh:github.com\",\n        \"observed\": \"keychain item readable\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"root\": {\n    \"nodeId\": \"645\",\n    \"author\": \"jcfischer\"\n  },\n  \"reasons\": [\n    \"credentials other than jcfischer are reachable from this session: keychain:gh:github.com\",\n    \"no ratification found — nothing was attested by a second credential\",\n    \"no proposal comment recorded — there is nothing for a ratification to bind to\",\n    \"graph root 645 is authored by the acting identity (jcfischer)\"\n  ]\n}\n```";

export const RECEIPT_0_18_0_ISSUE_648 = "## Resolution\n\n## Resolution — W1 frozen-artifact contract\n\nThe principal ratified a deliberately lightweight W1 contract. Its purpose is to\nmake Soma's existing fail-closed controls truthful and recoverable, not to build a\nsupply-chain security system.\n\n### 1. Enforcement artifact\n\nAn **enforcement artifact** is an immutable, versioned runtime directory under\n`~/.soma/runtime/<hash>/`. Substrate policy hooks point to that directory, never\nto an editable Soma repository or a general projection. The artifact is staged and\nload-checked by `soma install … --apply` before its hook configuration becomes\nactive.\n\nW1 does **not** hash or verify every artifact file on every hook invocation. A\nmissing or unloadable configured artifact fails the guarded operation closed.\n`soma doctor` and install report/validate the artifact identity; no network or\nGit freshness check belongs on the tool-call path.\n\n### 2. Activation and recovery\n\nInstall stages a new artifact, validates that it loads, atomically changes the hook\nconfiguration to it, and retains the preceding artifact. Rollback is an explicit,\nlocal switch back to the retained prior artifact. It is neither automatic nor the\nwhole-home `soma rollback` operation.\n\nA guard-load failure remains fail-closed, but its recovery guidance must name the\ninstalled-artifact repair/switch path; repairing a broken checkout must not require\nthat checkout to authorize the repair.\n\n### 3. Completion truth\n\nGitHub tracker state and Soma completion are distinct. A work-graph node is\n**Soma-complete** only when the authoritative close write has a receipt produced by\n`soma graph close`. Tracker auto-closes without a receipt are visible exceptions,\nnot successful completion; no automatic reopener is introduced. A principal can\nreconcile one explicitly by reopening and closing through the graph verb, or by\nrecording a reasoned ratification.\n\n### 4. Private roots\n\nW1 keeps the existing loader-safe private-root builders. It adds a cross-substrate\ndrift test proving the install spec, projected hook configuration, and policy\nevaluation resolve the identical roots. W1 does not redesign adapters or reintroduce\nthe installer import graph into Pi.dev.\n\n### Acceptance bar\n\n1. A deliberately broken editable Soma checkout does not affect a guard using the\n   last installed enforcement artifact; a policy denial still denies.\n2. A missing or unloadable configured artifact fails closed and gives a concrete\n   recovery message.\n3. A new artifact is load-checked before an atomic activation; explicitly switching\n   to the retained prior artifact restores its guard behavior.\n4. A receipt-less GitHub auto-close is not accepted as Soma-complete by any\n   completion consumer.\n5. Every substrate's install spec, hook config, and policy evaluation agree on its\n   private roots.\n\n### Deferred\n\nPer-invocation cryptographic artifact hashing, automatic rollback, a network/Git\nfreshness check on tool calls, automatic tracker reopening, and an adapter\narchitecture redesign are outside W1.\n\n## Close receipt\n\n- **checkpoint:** `cp-evolution-w1-contract`\n- **gist:** W1 uses a lightweight immutable runtime under ~/.soma/runtime/<hash>, staged/load-checked/atomically switched with explicit rollback; receipts—not tracker state—mean complete; private-root drift becomes a cross-substrate test.\n- **closed by:** jcfischer\n- **closed with:** soma 0.18.0 @ 45b9f1d (dev tree)\n- **at:** 2026-08-24T18:56:30.774Z\n- **attestation:** `unverified`\n\n### Evidence\n\n\n### Attestation facts\n\n```json\n{\n  \"backendCapability\": \"verifiable\",\n  \"confinement\": {\n    \"checked\": true,\n    \"reachableIdentities\": [\n      \"jcfischer\",\n      \"keychain:gh:github.com\"\n    ],\n    \"at\": \"2026-08-24T18:56:30.135Z\",\n    \"probes\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"gh auth status (token env stripped)\",\n        \"observed\": \"exit 0; identities: jcfischer\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"gh auth token (token env stripped)\",\n        \"observed\": \"printed a credential\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"security find-generic-password -s gh:github.com\",\n        \"observed\": \"keychain item readable\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"root\": {\n    \"nodeId\": \"645\",\n    \"author\": \"jcfischer\"\n  },\n  \"reasons\": [\n    \"credentials other than jcfischer are reachable from this session: keychain:gh:github.com\",\n    \"no ratification found — nothing was attested by a second credential\",\n    \"no proposal comment recorded — there is nothing for a ratification to bind to\",\n    \"graph root 645 is authored by the acting identity (jcfischer)\"\n  ]\n}\n```";
